---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const faqs = [
  ['What is the main reason firms look for a Digits alternative?', 'Digits is an AI-native new general ledger. Firms whose clients must stay on QuickBooks Online or Xero, or whose clients are outside the US, usually need a tool that works on the existing ledger instead.'],
  ['Which Digits alternative keeps clients on QuickBooks Online or Xero?', 'Booke AI does AI bookkeeping inside existing QBO/Xero files; its Business plan lists $129/business/month, with firm pricing by quote. Double and Xenett add a close and review layer on QBO.'],
  ['What is the cheapest published price among these alternatives?', 'Xenett AI Financials Review lists $7.50/client/month and Workflow $10/client/month (USD). Truewind and firm plans for Booke AI are by quote, and Double plan prices are behind a demo.'],
  ['Is Docyt a direct Digits replacement?', 'Only partly. Docyt focuses on hospitality and multi-location businesses, priced per property by quote, so it is not a generic swap for a small-business firm.'],
];
const faqLd = JSON.stringify({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqs.map(([q, a]) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: a } })),
});
---
<Base
  title="Digits alternatives for bookkeeping firms — keep QBO/Xero or go elsewhere"
  description="Looking past Digits’ AI-native ledger? Compare Booke AI, Truewind, Double, Xenett, Botkeeper, and Docyt for firms that stay on QBO/Xero or need non-US clients. Pricing verified Oct 2026."
>
  <h1>Digits alternatives</h1>
  <p>Firms leave or skip Digits when clients must stay on existing QuickBooks Online or Xero ledgers (Digits is an AI-native new GL), when clients are outside the US, when they want per-seat or existing-stack tools, or when Digits’ per-client tiers don’t fit. Below are the closest options in our directory — not a full market scan.</p>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Alternative</th>
        <th>Best fit vs Digits</th>
        <th>Pricing (verified Oct 2026)</th>
        <th>Trade-off</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/tools/booke-ai`}>Booke AI</a></td>
        <td>AI bookkeeping inside existing QBO/Xero files — not a new ledger</td>
        <td>Business $129/business/mo; firm/white-label by quote</td>
        <td>Layer on the client’s ledger; no Digits-style continuous native GL or firm free-books model</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/tools/truewind`}>Truewind</a></td>
        <td>AI month-end / bookkeeping for startups and firms</td>
        <td>By quote</td>
        <td>No published price card; sales-led vs Digits’ transparent per-client tiers</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/tools/double`}>Double (formerly Keeper)</a></td>
        <td>Close and automation layer on the existing QBO stack</td>
        <td>Per-client mix-and-match plans; demo required</td>
        <td>QBO-focused close/review — not a replacement GL; plan prices behind demo</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/tools/xenett`}>Xenett</a></td>
        <td>Review/close layer on QBO — flags P&amp;L and Balance Sheet issues</td>
        <td>AI Financials Review $7.50/client/mo; Workflow $10/client/mo (USD); add-ons e.g. Accruals + AI $15/client/mo</td>
        <td>Review and workflow on top of QBO, not 24/7 native bookkeeping or a new ledger</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/tools/botkeeper`}>Botkeeper Infinite</a></td>
        <td>Firm platform / categorization (Infinite under Xendoo)</td>
        <td>From $149/license/mo (volume down to $59 at 25+)</td>
        <td>License/volume model and firm tooling vs Digits per-client no-seat pricing; not an AI-native GL</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/tools/docyt`}>Docyt</a></td>
        <td>Partial overlap only: AI-native continuous close — hospitality / multi-location focus</td>
        <td>Per property, quote-only; unlimited users</td>
        <td>Not a generic SMB firm swap; priced per property for hotels/retail multi-unit</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>When Booke AI (or Double / Xenett) fits better</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Clients must keep QuickBooks Online or Xero as the system of record.</li>
    <li>You want AI categorization, exception review, or a close/review layer on the existing stack.</li>
    <li>You prefer a published per-business or per-client add-on price without migrating the GL.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>When to stay on Digits</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You’re willing to run clients on Digits’ AI-native general ledger instead of QBO/Xero.</li>
    <li>US-only entities; per-client Essentials/Core/Pro with no seat fees fits the firm model.</li>
    <li>You want continuous recon, Agentic Close, and firm free books in one product.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>When Truewind, Botkeeper, or Docyt instead</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Truewind: close-complexity and workflow depth matter more than a published price card; expect a quote.</li>
    <li>Botkeeper Infinite: you want firm-platform tooling (Close Tracker, volume licenses) on categorization, not a new ledger.</li>
    <li>Docyt: hospitality or multi-location retail/franchise books priced per property — partial overlap only.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>FAQ</h2>
  {faqs.map(([q, a]) => (<><h3>{q}</h3><p>{a}</p></>))}
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={faqLd} />

  <p>
    <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/compare/docyt-vs-digits-vs-truewind`}>Docyt vs Digits vs Truewind</a>
    · <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/tools/digits`}>Digits</a>
    · <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/category/month-end-close`}>All month-end close tools</a>
    · <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/compare/bank-reconciliation-tools`}>Bank reconciliation tools</a>
  </p>
</Base>

<style>
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 1rem 0; font-size: 0.95rem; }
  th, td { border: 1px solid #ddd; padding: 0.5rem 0.6rem; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }
  th { background: #f6f6f6; }
</style>
